WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
In the last video, the settled hydrogen iodide

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.120
tube gave us K: 0.70 squared, over 0.10

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.600
times 0.10, is 49.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.040
That was type one, with every concentration given.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.120
This video is type three.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.360
The question gives you K and the starting

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.960
concentrations, and nothing at equilibrium is measured.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.560
So there is no value to write in

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.120
the equilibrium row, and the change has to

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.080
be an unknown.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.580
Now the other way round.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.220
We know K and the start, and want

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.900
the settled concentrations.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.860
This is the hot hydrogen and iodine tube

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.740
from the catalyst and expressions videos, where K

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.860
is 49.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.100
Each dot is 0.05 moles per litre, so

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.060
the start is 0.45 moles per litre of

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.420
hydrogen, 0.45 of iodine and no hydrogen iodide.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.273
We don't know how much reacts, so call

00:00:58.314 --> 00:01:00.913
the amount of hydrogen used up x, in

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.033
moles per litre.

00:01:02.594 --> 00:01:05.473
The equation, H two plus I two making

00:01:05.554 --> 00:01:07.393
two H I, gives the rest.

00:01:07.954 --> 00:01:10.993
For each hydrogen used, one iodine is used

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.633
and two hydrogen iodide are made.

00:01:14.114 --> 00:01:16.993
So the change row is minus x, minus

00:01:17.074 --> 00:01:19.073
x and plus two x.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.140
The equilibrium row is initial plus change: 0.45

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:28.300
minus x for hydrogen and for iodine, and

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.380
two x for hydrogen iodide.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.220
Substitute into K.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.380
Hydrogen iodide squared is two x all squared,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.980
over hydrogen times iodine, and both of those

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.660
are 0.45 minus x, so the bottom is

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.180
0.45 minus x, all squared.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.100
That equals 49.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.860
The top is squared and the bottom is

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.980
squared, so the whole fraction is squared: two

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.140
x over 0.45 minus x, all squared, equals

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.420
49.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.460
Something squared equals a square number, a perfect

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.740
square, and 49 is seven squared.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.300
So take the square root of both sides:

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.460
two x over 0.45 minus x equals seven.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.900
Hydrogen iodide and hydrogen are both positive, so

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.540
this ratio is positive and we keep plus

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.100
seven.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.500
Now rearrange.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.460
Multiply both sides by 0.45 minus x: two

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.860
x equals 7 times 0.45 minus x, which

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.580
is 3.15 minus 7x.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.940
Add 7x to both sides, so nine x

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.020
equals 3.15.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.220
Find x.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.900
Pause here and try it.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.940
x is 0.35.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.340
So hydrogen and iodine are each 0.45 minus

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:04.380
0.35, 0.10 moles per litre, and hydrogen

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.740
iodide is two times 0.35, 0.70.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.820
Check by substituting back: 0.70 squared is 0.49,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:22.060
over 0.10 times 0.10, which is 0.010,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.660
gives 49.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.340
Why not minus seven?

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.780
That would need x of 0.63, more than

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.140
the 0.45 we started with, so hydrogen would

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.020
be negative.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.433
Here is the habit.

00:03:35.754 --> 00:03:39.273
Only the change row follows the coefficients: minus

00:03:39.354 --> 00:03:45.193
0.35, minus 0.35 and plus 0.70 are

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.753
in the ratio one, one, two.

00:03:48.074 --> 00:03:50.633
The initial and equilibrium rows do not have

00:03:50.674 --> 00:03:55.353
to be in that ratio: 0.10, 0.10 and

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.433
0.70 are not.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.193
Why did the square root work so neatly?

00:04:01.514 --> 00:04:04.793
Hydrogen and iodine started equal, so the bottom

00:04:04.874 --> 00:04:08.473
of the fraction was 0.45 minus x, times

00:04:08.594 --> 00:04:11.593
itself, a square, just like the top.

00:04:11.674 --> 00:04:13.353
K does not have to be a square

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:14.233
number.

00:04:14.314 --> 00:04:16.233
If K were 50, the root would be

00:04:16.314 --> 00:04:20.153
about 7.07, and the method would still work.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.833
What it needs is a top and a

00:04:22.034 --> 00:04:24.393
bottom that are both squares, so the whole

00:04:24.474 --> 00:04:26.793
fraction is something squared.

00:04:26.954 --> 00:04:28.873
That is what a perfect square means from

00:04:28.954 --> 00:04:32.273
now on: the fraction, not the number K.

00:04:32.714 --> 00:04:34.953
Many questions are not built like that, and

00:04:35.034 --> 00:04:37.193
the most common other case is a tiny

00:04:37.274 --> 00:04:37.673
K.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.540
Here is iodine again, on its own and

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.780
very hot.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.940
A few I two molecules split into iodine

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.980
atoms: I two makes two I.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.900
K is tiny: take it as 1.6 times

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.060
ten to the minus five, and we start

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.180
with 0.25 moles per litre of I two

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.820
and no atoms.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.340
Call the I two that splits x.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.460
Each I two makes two atoms, so the

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.100
change row is minus x and plus two

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.100
x, and the equilibrium row is 0.25 minus

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.540
x and two x.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.580
So K is two x all squared, over

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.900
0.25 minus x.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.420
The bottom is not a square, so the

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.940
square root will not help.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.020
But look at the size of K.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.140
A tiny K means hardly any I two

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.300
splits, so x is tiny next to 0.25.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.900
Taking a tiny amount from 0.25 still leaves

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:40.100
about 0.25, so we drop the x from

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.060
the bottom.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.060
Keep the x on top, because that is

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.660
the answer we want.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.500
This shortcut needs two things: K very small,

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.580
and a start that is not tiny.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.400
Now the equation is easy.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.520
Two x all squared is four x squared.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.600
Dividing by 0.25 is the same as multiplying

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.400
by four, so the left side is sixteen

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.360
x squared.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.560
That equals 1.6 times ten to the minus

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:11.640
five, so divide both sides by sixteen: x

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.520
squared is 1.0 times ten to the minus

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:19.160
six, and x is 0.0010 moles

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.120
per litre.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:25.000
The iodine atoms are two x, 0.0020 moles

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.320
per litre, and the I two is still

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.240
about 0.25.

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.706
Now check that dropping x was fair.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:39.506
x is 0.0010, and 0.0010 out

00:06:39.587 --> 00:06:43.146
of 0.25 is 0.4 per cent.

00:06:43.427 --> 00:06:45.346
The usual rule of thumb is that x

00:06:45.427 --> 00:06:47.186
should be under about 5 per cent of

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:50.066
the start, so the shortcut is safe.

00:06:50.307 --> 00:06:52.066
With a K this small and a normal

00:06:52.147 --> 00:06:54.306
start, it passes easily.

00:06:54.627 --> 00:06:59.266
Substitute back to be sure: 0.0020 squared

00:06:59.507 --> 00:07:02.706
is 4.0 times ten to the minus six,

00:07:02.787 --> 00:07:06.866
over 0.25, gives 1.6 times ten to the

00:07:06.947 --> 00:07:07.986
minus five.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.480
Notice what we never needed: the quadratic formula.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.720
You can use it if you like, but

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.440
HSC questions are written so you shouldn't need

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:17.680
it.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.080
When K and a start give you an

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.560
equation in x, look for one of two

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.360
things.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.800
Is it a perfect square?

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.160
Take the square root.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.720
Is K tiny, with a start that is

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.120
not?

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.440
Drop the x, then check it.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:33.586
Your turn.

00:07:33.867 --> 00:07:37.066
In a very hot engine, nitrogen and oxygen

00:07:37.147 --> 00:07:40.426
make a little nitrogen monoxide: N two plus

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:43.106
O two makes two N O.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:46.746
At this temperature K is 4.0 times ten

00:07:46.827 --> 00:07:48.426
to the minus four.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.866
The gases start at 0.50 moles per litre

00:07:51.947 --> 00:07:56.426
of nitrogen, 0.50 of oxygen, and no N

00:07:56.507 --> 00:07:57.066
O.

00:07:57.387 --> 00:08:00.466
Find the concentration of N O at equilibrium.

00:08:00.747 --> 00:08:02.026
Pause here to answer.

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:15.713
Nitrogen and oxygen each fall by x, and

00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:19.393
N O rises by two x, so K

00:08:19.554 --> 00:08:23.553
is two x all squared, over 0.50 minus

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:24.753
x, all squared.

00:08:25.394 --> 00:08:27.153
You could use either shortcut here.

00:08:27.634 --> 00:08:29.473
The starts are equal, so it is a

00:08:29.554 --> 00:08:32.593
perfect square: take the square root, and two

00:08:32.674 --> 00:08:38.273
x over 0.50 minus x is 0.020.

00:08:38.314 --> 00:08:43.473
Rearrange as before, and x is 0.00495,

00:08:43.554 --> 00:08:48.273
so N O is 0.0099 moles per litre.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.700
Or K is tiny, so drop the x:

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:57.420
the bottom becomes 0.50 times 0.50,

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.180
which is 0.25, and four x squared over

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:05.100
0.25 is sixteen x squared, which equals 4.0

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.980
times ten to the minus four.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.860
x squared is 2.5 times ten to the

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:15.500
minus five, x is 0.0050,

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.380
and N O is 0.010.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.500
Check it: x is about 1 per cent

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.260
of 0.50, well under 5 per cent, so

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.500
the shortcut is safe, and the two answers

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.340
agree to about 1 per cent.

00:09:30.567 --> 00:09:35.126
If you got 0.0050, that is x,

00:09:35.247 --> 00:09:37.286
but N O is two x.

00:09:37.607 --> 00:09:41.318
If you got 0.014, you put 0.50 on

00:09:41.527 --> 00:09:47.126
the bottom instead of 0.50 times 0.50.

00:09:47.167 --> 00:09:48.806
And if you wrote plus x for N

00:09:48.887 --> 00:09:51.766
O, look at the coefficient: two N O

00:09:51.847 --> 00:09:53.126
are made each time.

00:09:54.334 --> 00:09:57.213
So, for a type three question: call the

00:09:57.294 --> 00:09:59.893
change x, write the change row from the

00:09:59.934 --> 00:10:03.373
coefficients, add to get the equilibrium row, and

00:10:03.454 --> 00:10:04.733
substitute into K.

00:10:05.294 --> 00:10:06.733
Then look for a shortcut.

00:10:07.134 --> 00:10:09.693
A perfect square: take the square root and

00:10:09.774 --> 00:10:10.893
keep the positive root.

00:10:11.294 --> 00:10:14.013
A tiny K: drop the x, and check

00:10:14.054 --> 00:10:15.693
it is under about 5 per cent of

00:10:15.774 --> 00:10:16.333
the start.

00:10:16.734 --> 00:10:18.973
Either way, substitute back to check.

00:10:19.694 --> 00:10:23.453
Next: why factories do not wait for equilibrium.

00:10:24.667 --> 00:10:26.106
Here are the key notes.

00:10:26.347 --> 00:10:28.266
Pause the video if you need more time

00:10:28.347 --> 00:10:29.146
to copy them.
